# {repo_name}

Kairos v5 ontology hub for **{description}**.

## Quick start

```bash
uv sync
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --check
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --explain
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --emit ontology-hub/output/medallion/dbt
```

`--check` and `--explain` are write-free. `--emit` atomically writes only
manifest-owned artifacts. Compilation creates one immutable `CompilePlan` used by check,
explain, emit, and optional Gold/MDM consumers.

## Canonical authored inputs

```text
ontology-hub/
├── kairos.yaml                         # adapter: fabric | databricks
├── catalog-v001.xml
├── model/
│   ├── ontologies/                     # canonical TTL
│   ├── shapes/                         # optional SHACL
│   └── extensions/                     # optional Gold/MDM policy only
├── integration/
│   ├── sources/                        # authoritative source-vocabulary TTL
│   ├── bindings/                       # one closed EntityBinding per source
│   ├── discovery/                      # confirmed business context
│   └── transforms/dbt/models/          # optional ordinary SQL/YAML
└── output/                             # generated; do not edit
```

Claims, authored preparation policy, lifecycle/readiness state, release evidence, and
Silver-extension policy are not v5 authorities.

## Downstream use

Publish emitted artifacts at an immutable revision, pin that revision in the dataplatform,
then run `dbt deps`, `dbt parse`, `dbt build`, and `dbt test`. Never edit generated files.

## Toolkit updates

```bash
uv run kairos-ontology update --check
uv run kairos-ontology update --test-ref <branch-or-sha>
uv run kairos-ontology update --restore
```

Unreleased-ref testing is reversible and does not publish a release. V5 has no v4
compatibility or migration path; rebuild older hubs from this lean scaffold.
